aseline run confirms that `checkout.py` has a **deliberate defect**: it ignores the `quantity` field entirely.\n\n### What the current (broken) code does\n\n```python\nsubtotal = sum(price for price, quantity in items)  # quantity is IGNORED\nreturn subtotal + 5\n```\n\nIt only sums `unit_price` for each item, discarding `quantity`, then blindly adds 5.\n\n### Test-by-test breakdown\n\n| Items | Expected | Actual | Pass? | Why it fails |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `[(10, 2), (5, 1)]` | `(10×2 + 5×1) + 5 = 30` | `(10 + 5) + 5 = 20` | ❌ | Quantities 2 and 1 ignored |\n| `[(25, 2)]` | `(25×2) + 5 = 55` wait → `50` | `25 + 5 = 30` | ❌ | Quantity 2 ignored |\n| `[(49, 1)]` | `(49×1) + 5 = 54` | `49 + 5 = 54` | ✅ | Happens to pass because quantity=1 means `price×1 == price` |\n\nThe third test passes **by accident** — when `quantity=1`, multiplying by quantity makes no difference, so the bug is invisible.\n\n### Root cause\n\nLine 4 of [`checkout.py`](file:///Users/xxxxx/Repository/session-bench/artifacts/v1-expanded-preparation/live-captures/antigravity-2026-10-05-03/workspace/fixture_project/checkout.py#L4) should be:\n\n```python\nsubtotal = sum(price * quantity for price, quantity in items)\n```\n\nBut the task instructs me not to edit `checkout.py` yet — stopping here as instructed.\n\nSB_SURVIVAL_V1_RESPONSE_R1_cafe_🙂","turn_id":"turn-r1"},"id":"response-r1","kind":"assistant_response","metric_ids":["work.visible_responses","causal.turn_response","attribution.model_config","attribution.usage","attribution.token_semantics"],"population_role":"primary_scored","sequence":7,"session_id":"c61c209c-78a0-432a-a4c1-4e503a99d9f0","source":"visible_stream"},{"boundary":"accepted","fields":{"response_canary":"SB_SURVIVAL_V1_RESPONSE_R2_correction_Δ","revision":"r2","role":"user","run_canary":"SB_SURVIVAL_V1_RUN_antigravity-2026-10-05-03","text":"Correction R2 supersedes only the delivery condition: delivery is free when subtotal is at least 50 and remains 5 below 50. Keep quant